# Line endings that are not a matter of taste.
#
# This is a Windows-first repo, so a checkout hands most files CRLF and that is
# right for them. Two kinds of file break if they get it, and both are load
# bearing now that CI runs on Linux:
#
#   gradlew is a shell script. With CRLF, Linux reads the carriage return as
#   part of the interpreter path and fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" —
#   a message that says nothing about line endings to anyone who has not met it
#   before.
#
#   .bat is the exact opposite: cmd wants CRLF, and test.bat is what a person
#   double-clicks.
#
# Left deliberately narrow. A repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise
# every tracked file in one commit, which is a large diff that hides whatever
# else is in it, to fix a problem only these files have.

android/gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never line-ending-convert the wrapper jar. Git detects this on its own, but
# the failure if it ever did not is a corrupt jar and an unbuildable app, so it
# is worth one line to state rather than infer.
*.jar binary
